ession with typed inputs and try it with function_try(source, params); direct primitive calls are impossible in this mode. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines}, and listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans le code source de ce workspace, comment le répertoire .tours/.memory persiste-t-il les procédures du harness de recherche ? Détermine le format de stockage des procédures, l'identité d'une procédure demée (structure du fichier), le chemin exact et le moment d'écriture, ainsi que les conditions de validation ou de refus de persistance d'une fonction. Produis un résultat structuré JSON avec, pour chaque fait, une référence fichier:ligne (les sources réelles, pas des ancres inventées)."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"gx2WwfBdt","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"function listFiles() { return listFiles(); }\\nconst rootFiles = listFiles();\\nconsole.log(\\\"Root files:\\\", rootFiles);\\nreturn rootFiles;\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"list_root_files\",\"question\":\"List all files in the repository root to identify presence of .tours/.memory directory\",\"description\":\"Lists files at repository root to confirm existence and structure of .tours/.memory directory\",\"returns\":\"Array of file paths at repository root\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"gx2WwfBdt","content":"{\"error\":\"TS2384:1:Overload signatures must all be ambient or non-ambient.\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"Mw9X7iWTo","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"() => listFiles()\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"list_root_files\",\"question\":\"List all files in the repository root to identify presence of .tours/.memory directory\",\"description\":\"Lists files at repository root to confirm existence and structure of .tours/.memory directory\",\"returns\":\"Array of file paths at repository root\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Mw9X7iWTo","content":"{\"result\":[\".npmrc\",\"benchmarks/query-probe.mjs\",\"dist/citation-validator.js\",\"dist/cli.js\",\"dist/decomposition-prompt.js\",\"dist/exploration-evidence.js\",\"dist/exploration-helpers.js\",\"dist/explore.js\",\"dist/memory-output.js\",\"dist/memory.js\",\"dist/mistral.js\",\"dist/primitives.js\",\"dist/research-log.js\",\"dist/tool-contract.js\",\"dist/workspace.js\",\"package-lock.json\",\"package.json\",\"README.md\",\"skills/codetour-research/SKILL.md\",\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"src/cli.ts\",\"src/decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"src/exploration-evidence.ts\",\"src/exploration-helpers.ts\",\"src/explore.ts\",\"src/memory-output.ts\",\"src