 Wrapping obligation: the ten permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are NOT exposed as direct tools — they are only callable inside a function_try source. Wrap the primitives a question needs in one TypeScript function expression with typed inputs and try it with function_try(source, params); direct primitive calls are impossible in this mode. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines}, and listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans ce workspace, comment fonctionne la réutilisation de la mémoire de procédures via memory_run ? Détermine : (1) comment une procédure persistée est retrouvée et appariée à une nouvelle question (identité, sélection, fichier src/memory.ts et src/memory-output.ts), (2) comment elle est exécutée et rejouée (function_try, replay), et (3) quelle preuve structurée atteste que la sortie d'une procédure rejouée a été pertinente et utilisée. Produis un JSON structuré avec des références fichier:ligne réelles du workspace."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"8qczpohFE","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"function searchToursMemoryPath(): { file: string; line: number; context: string }[] {\\n  // Search the entire workspace for any occurrence of the string '.tours/.memory'\\n  const matches: { file: string; line: number; context: string }[] = [];\\n  const files = listFiles();\\n  for (const file of files) {\\n    if (!file.endsWith('.ts') && !file.endsWith('.js')) continue;\\n    try {\\n      const lines = readLines(file, 1, 100000);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\\n        const line = lines[i];\\n        if (line.text.includes('.tours/.memory')) {\\n          matches.push({ file: file, line: line.start, context: line.text.trim() });\\n        }\\n      }\\n    } catch {\\n      // Skip files that can't be read\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return matches;\\n}\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"search_tours_memory_path\",\"question\":\"Find all references to the path .tours/.memory in the codebase to confirm its existence and usage\",\"description\":\"Searches the entire codebase for any occurrence of the string '.tours/.memory' to identify files that reference this directory and understand its role\",\"returns\":\"Array of { file: string; line: number; context: string } where each entry is a line containing '.tours/.memory' with its file path, line number, and the line content.\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"8qczpohFE","content":"{\"error\":\"TS2339:9:Property 'length' does not exist on t