emory\\\");\"},{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"line\":39,\"context\":\"La mémoire activée par `--memory` reste propre au projet dans `.tours/.memory/` ; les journaux structurés sont dans `.tours/.log/`. Les fichiers `.tour` existants sont conservés. Lancer les questions séquentiellement : le catalogue ne garantit pas les écritures concurrentes. Les références valides prouvent l'existence des lignes, pas la justesse sémantique de l'explication. Le harnais répond à des questions et ne crée pas de Tour.\"},{\"file\":\"skills/codetour-research/SKILL.md\",\"line\":25,\"context\":\"Pass the actual absolute root and one question as separate, safely quoted arguments; do not interpolate user text into shell syntax. Wait for each JSON result before starting the next call. Use the same workspace so all calls share `.tours/.memory/`. If a result is partial or failed, retain its status and uncertainties; request a targeted follow-up only for a gap that matters, or explain the limitation. Do not repeat a sufficient answer. Direct file reads are allowed for targeted verification; record what was checked and why. Substantial research belongs in the harness.\"}],\"returned\":6,\"observed\":6,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":2577,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"UcFjtRNOx","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"function listRelevantFiles(): string[] {\\n  // List files in src/ and related directories to confirm presence of memory-related files\\n  const files = listFiles();\\n  const relevant = files.filter(f => \\n    f.startsWith('src/') && \\n    (f.includes('memory') || f.includes('replay') || f.includes('function_try'))\\n  );\\n  return relevant;\\n}\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"list_relev