duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selectio\"},{\"file\":\"dist/memory-output.js\",\"line\":3,\"context\":\"* calls (memory_run / function_try).\"},{\"file\":\"dist/memory.js\",\"line\":212,\"context\":\"memory_run: (id, params = {}) => {\"},{\"file\":\"dist/mistral.js\",\"line\":21,\"context\":\"{ type: 'function', function: { name: 'memory_run', description: 'Run a stored script with new parameters against the current workspace.', parameters: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, params: { type: 'object' } }, required: ['id', 'params'] } } },\"},{\"file\":\"dist/mistral.js\",\"line\":94,\"context\":\"? { id: call.id, name: 'memory_run', arguments: { id: named.id, params: Object.fromEntries(named.parameters.filter(parameter => args[parameter] !== undefined).map(parameter => [parameter, args[parameter]])) } }\"},{\"file\":\"skills/codetour-research/SKILL.md\",\"line\":28,\"context\":\"5. In that report separate observed facts, inferences and unmeasurable information. Use Copilot tool history to identify direct reads when available; otherwise mark direct research **not measurable**, never zero. Assess delegation separately from Tour quality: substantial research performed mainly outside the harness fails delegation even if a Tour was written. Structural citation validation establishes that lines exist, not that their interpretation is correct; identify semantic review as a separate check. For each persisted function, inspect its source and observed output when available: state the recurring question it addresses and the structured evidence it actually produces. Do not claim useful learning from persistence alone: require a later `memory_run` execution of the same identity and evidence that its output was relevant to the later question. Do not force a function into memory when none is useful. Include an honest outcome when evidence or telemetry is missing.\"},{\"file\":\"src/decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"line\":4,\"context\":\"export const DECOMPOSITION_PROMPT = 'Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties.';\"},{\"file\":\"src/exploration-helpers.ts\",\"line\":28,\"context\":\"type: 'model' | 'tool' | 'memory_run' | 'memory_list' | 'function_try' | 'decomposition_plan' | 'decomposition_decision' | 'run_end';\"},{\"file\":\"src/explore.ts\",\"line\":214,\"context\":\"let scriptCall: { type: 'memory_run' | 'function_try'; name: string } | undefined;\"},{\"file\":\"src/explore.ts\",\"line\":265,\"context\":\"else if (codeMode && ((call.name === 'code' && typeof call.arguments.code === 'string') || (call.name === 'function_try' && typeof call.arguments.source === 'string') || (library && call.name === 'memory_run' && typeof call.arguments.id === 'string'))) {\"},{\"file\":\"src/explore.ts\",\"line\":266,\"context\":\"const stored = call.name === 'memory_run' ? library?.get(String(call.arguments.id)) : undefined;\"},{\"file\":\"src/explore.ts\",\"line\":267,\"context\":\"if (call.name === 'memory_run' && !stored) throw new Error('Unknown script');\"},{\"file\":\"src/explore.ts\",\"line\":276,\"context\":\"scriptCall = { type: stored ? 'memory_run' : 'function_try', name: stored ? stored.id : 'function_try' };\"},{\"file\":\"src/explore.ts\",\"line\":277,\"context\":\"// Ticket #191: any memory_run/function_try call — accepted or failed —\"}],\"returned\":23,\"observed\