emory\\\");\"},{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"line\":39,\"context\":\"La mémoire activée par `--memory` reste propre au projet dans `.tours/.memory/` ; les journaux structurés sont dans `.tours/.log/`. Les fichiers `.tour` existants sont conservés. Lancer les questions séquentiellement : le catalogue ne garantit pas les écritures concurrentes. Les références valides prouvent l'existence des lignes, pas la justesse sémantique de l'explication. Le harnais répond à des questions et ne crée pas de Tour.\"},{\"file\":\"skills/codetour-research/SKILL.md\",\"line\":25,\"context\":\"Pass the actual absolute root and one question as separate, safely quoted arguments; do not interpolate user text into shell syntax. Wait for each JSON result before starting the next call. Use the same workspace so all calls share `.tours/.memory/`. If a result is partial or failed, retain its status and uncertainties; request a targeted follow-up only for a gap that matters, or explain the limitation. Do not repeat a sufficient answer. Direct file reads are allowed for targeted verification; record what was checked and why. Substantial research belongs in the harness.\"}],\"returned\":6,\"observed\":6,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":2577,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"UcFjtRNOx","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"function listRelevantFiles(): string[] {\\n  // List files in src/ and related directories to confirm presence of memory-related files\\n  const files = listFiles();\\n  const relevant = files.filter(f => \\n    f.startsWith('src/') && \\n    (f.includes('memory') || f.includes('replay') || f.includes('function_try'))\\n  );\\n  return relevant;\\n}\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"list_relevant_files\",\"question\":\"List TypeScript files in src/ related to memory, replay, and function_try to confirm their presence in the workspace\",\"description\":\"Lists files under src/ that are likely to contain the logic for memory persistence, matching, replay, and function_try to enable further analysis\",\"returns\":\"Array of file paths under src/ related to memory, replay, or function_try.\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"UcFjtRNOx","content":"{\"result\":[\"src/memory-output.ts\",\"src/memory.ts\"],\"returned\":2,\"observed\":2,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":40,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"Os1iuNEV3","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"function findMemoryRunReferences(): { file: string; line: number; context: string }[] {\\n  // Search for memory_run function calls or definitions\\n  const matches = searchText('memory_run');\\n  return matches.map(m => ({ file: m.file, line: m.line, context: m.text.trim() }));\\n}\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"find_memory_run_references\",\"question\":\"Find all references to memory_run in the codebase to understand its usage and parameters\",\"description\":\"Searches the entire codebase for any occurrence of 'memory_run' to identify how it is called and what parameters it expects\",\"returns\":\"Array of { file: string; line: number; context: string } where each entry is a line containing 'memory_run' with its file path, line number, and the line content.\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Os1iuNEV3","content":"{\"result\":[{\"file\":\"dist/decomposition-prompt.js\",\"line\":3,\"context\":\"export const DECOMPOSITION_PROMPT = 'Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties.';\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":277,\"context\":\"else if (codeMode && ((call.name === 'code' && typeof call.arguments.code === 'string') || (call.name === 'function_try' && typeof call.arguments.source === 'string') || (library && call.name === 'memory_run' && typeof call.arguments.id === 'string'))) {\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":278,\"context\":\"const stored = call.name === 'memory_run' ? library?.get(String(call.arguments.id)) : undefined;\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":279,\"context\":\"if (call.name === 'memory_run' && !stored)\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":291,\"context\":\"scriptCall = { type: stored ? 'memory_run' : 'function_try', name: stored ? stored.id : 'function_try' };\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":292,\"context\":\"// Ticket #191: any memory_run/function_try call — accepted or failed —\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":312,\"context\":\"// Compact, structured, bounded, sourced output for memory_run AND function_try.\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":364,\"context\":\"recordCall({ type: scriptCall?.type ?? 'function_try', name: call.name === 'memory_run' ? String(call.arguments.id ?? call.name) : 'function_try', callId: call.id, questionId, parameters: stored ? { id: stored.id, params } : undefined, inputTokens: null, outputTokens: null, usageMissing: false, error: String(error) }, runStarted, new Date());\"},{\"file\":\"dist/explore.js\",\"line\":388,\"context\"