duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selectio\"},{\"file\":\"dist/memory-output.js\",\"line\":3,\"context\":\"* calls (memory_run / function_try).\"},{\"file\":\"dist/memory.js\",\"line\":212,\"context\":\"memory_run: (id, params = {}) => {\"},{\"file\":\"dist/mistral.js\",\"line\":21,\"context\":\"{ type: 'function', function: { name: 'memory_run', description: 'Run a stored script with new parameters against the current workspace.', parameters: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, params: { type: 'object' } }, required: ['id', 'params'] } } },\"},{\"file\":\"dist/mistral.js\",\"line\":94,\"context\":\"? { id: call.id, name: 'memory_run', arguments: { id: named.id, params: Object.fromEntries(named.parameters.filter(parameter => args[parameter] !== undefined).map(parameter => [parameter, args[parameter]])) } }\"},{\"file\":\"skills/codetour-research/SKILL.md\",\"line\":28,\"context\":\"5. In that report separate observed facts, inferences and unmeasurable information. Use Copilot tool history to identify direct reads when available; otherwise mark direct research **not measurable**, never zero. Assess delegation separately from Tour quality: substantial research performed mainly outside the harness fails delegation even if a Tour was written. Structural citation validation establishes that lines exist, not that their interpretation is correct; identify semantic review as a separate check. For each persisted function, inspect its source and observed output when available: state the recurring question it addresses and the structured evidence it actually produces. Do not claim useful learning from persistence alone: require a later `memory_run` execution of the same identity and evidence that its output was relevant to the later question. Do not force a function into memory when none is useful. Include an honest outcome when evidence or telemetry is miss