{"level":30,"time":1794911230820,"pid":9072,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"959373e8-0a35-4020-971d-f721574890fe","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[{\"topic\":\"Rôle global du système de validation\",\"description\":\"Comprendre comment le harness de recherche valide les sorties et citations produites par les outils. Identifier le flux de données depuis l'exécution d'un outil jusqu'à la validation finale.\",\"references\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"line\":1},{\"file\":\"docs/architecture.md\",\"line\":10}]},{\"topic\":\"Concepts clés : citation-validator\",\"description\":\"Définir ce qu'est un 'citation-validator' dans ce contexte : règles de validation, format des citations attendues, mécanismes de refus.\",\"references\":[{\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":1}]},{\"topic\":\"Concepts clés : tool-contract\",\"description\":\"Comprendre le contrat imposé aux outils : signature de runScript, fonction stricte, timeout, et comment ces contraintes sont vérifiées.\",\"references\":[{\"file\":\"src/tool-contract.ts\",\"line\":1}]},{\"topic\":\"Mécanismes de sandboxing\",\"description\":\"Identifier les différents niveaux de sandbox : sandbox standard, exploration-sandbox, et comment ils limitent l'exécution des outils.\",\"references\":[{\"file\":\"src/sandbox.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"file\":\"src/exploration-sandbox.ts\",\"line\":1}]},{\"topic\":\"Historique d'outils et interaction\",\"description\":\"Comprendre comment l'historique d'outils (tool history) est utilisé par le citation-validator pour valider les citations et détecter les incohérences.\",\"references\":[{\"file\":\"src/tool-history.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":10}]},{\"topic\":\"Signalement des refus\",\"description\":\"Identifier les mécanismes de signalement des refus : exceptions, codes d'erreur, logs, et comment ils sont remontés à l'utilisateur ou au système.\",\"references\":[{\"file\":\"src/errors.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"file\":\"src/logger.ts\",\"line\":1}]}],\"investigate\":[{\"action\":\"Analyser le fichier src/citation-validator.ts\",\"description\":\"Lire le fichier pour comprendre les règles de validation, les motifs de refus, et comment il interagit avec l'historique d'outils.\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"Lister les fonctions exportées\",\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Identifier les règles de validation (ex: format des citations, vérification des sources)\",\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":10},{\"step\":\"Trouver les motifs de refus (ex: citation manquante, source non vérifiable)\",\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":30},{\"step\":\"Comprendre l'interaction avec l'historique d'outils (tool history)\",\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":50},{\"step\":\"Identifier les fonctions appelées depuis l'historique (ex: getToolHistory, validateCitation)\",\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":70}]},{\"action\":\"Analyser le fichier src/tool-contract.ts\",\"description\":\"Comprendre le contrat imposé aux outils : signature de runScript, fonction stricte, timeout, et vérifications associées.\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"Lister les interfaces et types définis (IToolContract, IRunScriptOptions)\",\"file\":\"src/tool-contract.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Identifier les contraintes imposées (ex: timeout par défaut, signature stricte de la fonction)\",\"file\":\"src/tool-contract.ts\",\"line\":20},{\"step\":\"Comprendre le mécanisme de validation du contrat (ex: zod schema, validation au runtime)\",\"file\":\"src/tool-contract.ts\",\"line\":40},{\"step\":\"Trouver les exemples d'outils conformes et non conformes\",\"file\":\"src/tool-contract.ts\",\"line\":60}]},{\"action\":\"Analyser le contrôle d'exécution réelle (sandbox et exploration-sandbox)\",\"description\":\"Comprendre comment l'exécution des outils est contrôlée via les mécanismes de sandboxing.\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"Lister les fonctions principales de sandbox.ts (ex: runInSandbox, applyRestrictions)\",\"file\":\"src/sandbox.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Identifier les restrictions appliquées (ex: accès au filesystem, réseau, timeout)\",\"file\":\"src/sandbox.ts\",\"line\":20},{\"step\":\"Lister les fonctions principales de exploration-sandbox.ts (ex: runInExplorationSandbox)\",\"file\":\"src/exploration-sandbox.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Comprendre les différences entre sandbox standard et exploration-sandbox\",\"file\":\"src/exploration-sandbox.ts\",\"line\":20},{\"step\":\"Trouver comment les outils sont wrappés avant exécution (ex: avecToolContract)\",\"file\":\"src/sandbox.ts\",\"line\":40}]},{\"action\":\"Identifier les refus d'écriture ou de consolidation\",\"description\":\"Trouver les cas où une sortie ou une citation est refusée, et comment ces refus sont signalés.\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"Rechercher les fonctions de refus dans le codebase (ex: rejectOutput, rejectConsolidation)\",\"file\":\"src/\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Trouver les codes d'erreur associés (ex: VALIDATION_ERROR, SANDBOX_TIMEOUT)\",\"file\":\"src/errors.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Comprendre le flux de signalement (ex: throw new ValidationError(), logger.error())\",\"file\":\"src/logger.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Identifier les points d'entrée où ces refus sont déclenchés (ex: dans citation-validator, dans sandbox)\",\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"line\":100}]},{\"action\":\"Vérifier l'existence et l'usage de .tours/.memory\",\"description\":\"Confirmer que le répertoire .tours/.memory existe et comprendre son rôle dans le système.\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"Rechercher les références à '.tours/.memory' dans le codebase\",\"file\":\"src/\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Identifier les fichiers qui lisent/écrivent dans ce répertoire\",\"file\":\"src/tool-history.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Comprendre son rôle : stockage de l'historique des outils, cache des citations, etc.\",\"file\":\"src/tool-history.ts\",\"line\":20}]},{\"action\":\"Comprendre l'usage de memory_run\",\"description\":\"Identifier comment memory_run est utilisé dans le système, notamment pour l'exécution des outils.\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"Rechercher les références à 'memory_run' dans le codebase\",\"file\":\"src/\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Trouver sa définition et ses paramètres (ex: memory_run(toolName, args, options))\",\"file\":\"src/memory-run.ts\",\"line\":1},{\"step\":\"Comprendre son intégration avec le contrat d'outil et la sandbox\",\"file\":\"src/memory-run.ts\",\"line\":20}]}],\"reuse\":[{\"id\":\"search_tours_memory_path\",\"purpose\":\"Vérifier l'existence et l'usage du répertoire .tours/.memory dans le codebase, qui pourrait être lié à l'historique des outils ou au stockage des citations.\",\"expectedOutput\":\"Liste des fichiers référençant '.tours/.memory' avec numéros de ligne pour comprendre son rôle.\"},{\"id\":\"find_memory_run_references\",\"purpose\":\"Comprendre comment memory_run est utilisé dans le système, notamment pour l'exécution des outils et son interaction avec le contrat d'outil et la sandbox.\",\"expectedOutput\":\"Liste des appels à memory_run avec contexte (fichier, ligne, extrait de code) pour analyser son intégration.\"}]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: [{\"id\":\"search_tours_memory_path\",\"objective\":\"Find all references to the path .tours/.memory in the codebase to confirm its existence and usage\",\"description\":\"Searches the entire codebase for any occurrence of the string '.tours/.memory' to identify files that reference this directory and understand its role\",\"parameters\":[],\"paramsSchema\":[],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"SourceMatch[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"},{\"id\":\"find_memory_run_references\",\"objective\":\"Find all references to memory_run in the codebase to understand its usage and parameters\",\"description\":\"Searches the entire codebase for any occurrence of 'memory_run' to identify how it is called and what parameters it expects\",\"parameters\":[],\"paramsSchema\":[],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; context: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. Wrapping obligation: the ten permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are NOT exposed as direct tools — they are only callable inside a function_try source. Wrap the primitives a question needs in one TypeScript function expression with typed inputs and try it with function_try(source, params); direct primitive calls are impossible in this mode. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines}, and listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans ce workspace, comment fonctionne la validation des sorties et des citations du harness de recherche ? Détermine : (1) ce que fait src/citation-validator.ts (règles, motifs de refus, interaction avec l'historique d'outils), (2) ce que le contrat src/tool-contract.ts impose aux outils (runScript, fonction stricte, timeout) et comment l'exécution réelle est contrôlée (sandbox, exploration-sandbox), (3) quels refus d'écriture ou de consolidation peuvent survenir et comment ils sont signalés. Produis un JSON structuré avec des références fichier:ligne réelles du workspace."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"0zweEnHz7","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"listFiles()\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"list_workspace_files\",\"question\":\"List all files in the workspace to identify relevant source files for analysis\",\"description\":\"Returns the list of files in the current workspace to help identify which source files to examine for the validation harness system\",\"returns\":\"string[]\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"0zweEnHz7","content":"{\"result\":[\".npmrc\",\".tours/.memory/8bbdd70ec3d478897e7fa877e6b7a0636f9efa28734ee963a1426d6094b40887.json\",\".tours/.memory/functions/find_memory_run_references.ts\",\".tours/.memory/functions/search_tours_memory_path.ts\",\"benchmarks/query-probe.mjs\",\"dist/citation-validator.js\",\"dist/cli.js\",\"dist/decomposition-prompt.js\",\"dist/exploration-evidence.js\",\"dist/exploration-helpers.js\",\"dist/explore.js\",\"dist/memory-output.js\",\"dist/memory.js\",\"dist/mistral.js\",\"dist/primitives.js\",\"dist/research-log.js\",\"dist/tool-contract.js\",\"dist/workspace.js\",\"package-lock.json\",\"package.json\",\"README.md\",\"skills/codetour-research/SKILL.md\",\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"src/cli.ts\",\"src/decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"src/exploration-evidence.ts\",\"src/exploration-helpers.ts\",\"src/explore.ts\",\"src/memory-output.ts\",\"src/memory.ts\",\"src/mistral.ts\",\"src/primitives.ts\",\"src/research-log.ts\",\"src/sandbox.d.ts\",\"src/tool-contract.ts\",\"src/workspace.ts\",\"test/citation-repair.test.ts\",\"test/citation-validator.test.ts\",\"test/cli.test.ts\",\"test/consolidation-d04.test.ts\",\"test/consolidation.test.ts\",\"test/empty-memory-list-note.test.ts\",\"test/explore.test.ts\",\"test/final-answer-fence-whitespace.test.ts\",\"test/final-answer-json-recovery.test.ts\",\"test/final-answer-recovery-visibility.test.ts\",\"test/finish-t02.test.ts\",\"test/fixture-explore.ts\",\"test/internal-instructions-english.test.ts\",\"test/memory.test.ts\"],\"returned\":50,\"observed\":61,\"truncated\":true,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":1388,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\",\"Output truncated to 50 items / 8000 bytes; it is NOT exhaustive. Re-run with narrower params to see the remainder.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"9lotBkQYg","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"readLines(\\\"src/citation-validator.ts\\\", 1, 120)\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"read_citation_validator\",\"question\":\"What does src/citation-validator.ts do regarding validation rules, refusal reasons, and interaction with tool history?\",\"description\":\"Reads the source of src/citation-validator.ts to extract exported functions, validation rules, refusal reasons, and how it interacts with tool history\",\"returns\":\"Lines of src/citation-validator.ts with file and line numbers\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"9lotBkQYg","content":"{\"error\":\"Script error: Invalid line range: use positive integer bounds and at most 100 lines\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"cqQEUqmHY","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"readLines(\\\"src/citation-validator.ts\\\", 1, 100)\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"read_citation_validator\",\"question\":\"What does src/citation-validator.ts do regarding validation rules, refusal reasons, and interaction with tool history?\",\"description\":\"Reads the source of src/citation-validator.ts to extract exported functions, validation rules, refusal reasons, and how it interacts with tool history\",\"returns\":\"Lines of src/citation-validator.ts with file and line numbers\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"cqQEUqmHY","content":"{\"result\":{\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"start\":1,\"lines\":[\"/**\",\" * Deterministic citation validation for function_try outputs\",\" * (issue #185, spec #183 — D02).\",\" *\",\" * Every mandatory reference a trial emits — any object carrying a `file`\",\" * field — is verified without any LLM: workspace confinement, file presence,\",\" * positive line bounds, startLine <= endLine, end within the real file, exact\",\" * excerpt equality when an excerpt is provided, and revision match when the\",\" * reference claims one. Partial validity is explicit: valid references stay\",\" * visible in the diagnostic and only the faulty ones are identified for\",\" * repair. The validator proves structural integrity only, never semantic\",\" * relevance — an existing citation is not proof of a business relation.\",\" */\",\"\",\"import { FileTooLargeError, PathOutsideWorkspaceError } from './primitives.ts';\",\"\",\"/** Confined read of the actual lines [startLine..endLine] plus the real total line count. */\",\"export interface CitationAccess {\",\"  readRange(file: string, startLine: number, endLine: number): Promise<{ lines: string[]; totalLines: number }>;\",\"}\",\"\",\"/** A single source reference: confined file path plus an exact line range. */\",\"export interface Reference {\",\"  file: string;\",\"  startLine: number;\",\"  endLine: number;\",\"}\",\"\",\"export interface InvalidCitation extends Partial<Reference> {\",\"  /** Short, structured, actionable error strings (type + path/line detail). */\",\"  errors: string[];\",\"}\",\"\",\"export interface CitationValidation {\",\"  /** 'valid' only when every emitted reference was verified; a failed trial is never treated as validated. */\",\"  status: 'valid' | 'validation_failed' | 'no_references';\",\"  /** Total mandatory references found in the output. */\",\"  references: number;\",\"  /** References actually verified (bounded by the safety ceiling). */\",\"  validated: number;\",\"  validCount: number;\",\"  /** Bounded list of the valid references (diagnostic visibility). */\",\"  validReferences: Reference[];\",\"  /** Bounded list of only the faulty references, for repair. */\",\"  invalidReferences: InvalidCitation[];\",\"  /** False when the ceiling stopped validation: the output is then NOT proven exhaustive. */\",\"  exhaustive: boolean;\",\"}\",\"\",\"/** Safety ceiling: at most this many references are verified per trial (configurable). */\",\"const MAX_REFERENCES = 300;\",\"/** Citation spans must fit a single confined read (workspace MAX_READ_LINES). */\",\"const MAX_SPAN_LINES = 100;\",\"/** Bounded diagnostic lists. */\",\"const MAX_LISTED = 10;\",\"/** Per-line excerpt truncation bounds of the permanent primitives (searchText/readLines: 2000, searchIdentifiers/findDefinitions: 500). */\",\"const EXCERPT_PREFIX_BOUNDS = [500, 2000];\",\"/** Fields that carry the reference's own excerpt — never recursed into as nested references. */\",\"const EXCERPT_KEYS = ['text', 'excerpt', 'lineText', 'lines'];\",\"\",\"/** Recursively collect every file-bearing object: those are the mandatory references. */\",\"function collectReferences(value: unknown, out: Record<string, unknown>[]): Record<string, unknown>[] {\",\"  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return out;\",\"  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\",\"    for (const child of value) collectReferences(child, out);\",\"    return out;\",\"  }\",\"  const record = value as Record<string, unknown>;\",\"  if (typeof record.file === 'string') out.push(record);\",\"  for (const [key, child] of Object.entries(record)) {\",\"    if (!EXCERPT_KEYS.includes(key)) collectReferences(child, out);\",\"  }\",\"  return out;\",\"}\",\"\",\"export async function validateCitations(value: unknown, options: { access: CitationAccess; revision?: string; maxReferences?: number }): Promise<CitationValidation> {\",\"  const references = collectReferences(value, []);\",\"  if (references.length === 0) {\",\"    return { status: 'no_references', references: 0, validated: 0, validCount: 0, validReferences: [], invalidReferences: [], exhaustive: true };\",\"  }\",\"  const ceiling = options.maxReferences ?? MAX_REFERENCES;\",\"  const invalid: InvalidCitation[] = [];\",\"  const valid: Reference[] = [];\",\"  let validated = 0;\",\"  for (const reference of references) {\",\"    if (validated >= ceiling) break;\",\"    validated++;\",\"    const check = await checkReference(reference, options);\",\"    if (check.invalid) invalid.push(check.invalid);\",\"    else valid.push(check.valid);\",\"  }\",\"  const exhaustive = validated === references.length;\",\"  if (!exhaustive) {\",\"    invalid.push({ errors: [`${references.length} references emitted; only ${validated} validated — the output is NOT proven exhaustive. Narrow the function output to at most ${ceiling} references and retry.`] });\",\"  }\",\"  return {\",\"    status: invalid.length > 0 ? 'validation_failed' : 'valid',\",\"    references: references.length,\",\"    validated,\",\"    validCount: valid.length,\"]},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":4856,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471