om another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans ce workspace, comment fonctionne la validation des sorties et des citations du harness de recherche ? Détermine : (1) ce que fait src/citation-validator.ts (règles, motifs de refus, interaction avec l'historique d'outils), (2) ce que le contrat src/tool-contract.ts impose aux outils (runScript, fonction stricte, timeout) et comment l'exécution réelle est contrôlée (sandbox, exploration-sandbox), (3) quels refus d'écriture ou de consolidation peuvent survenir et comment ils sont signalés. Produis un JSON structuré avec des références fichier:ligne réelles du workspace."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"0zweEnHz7","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"listFiles()\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"list_workspace_files\",\"question\":\"List all files in the workspace to identify relevant source files for analysis\",\"description\":\"Returns the list of files in the current workspace to help identify which source files to examine for the validation harness system\",\"returns\":\"string[]\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"0zweEnHz7","content":"{\"result\":[\".npmrc\",\".tours/.memory/8bbdd70ec3d478897e7fa877e6b7a0636f9efa28734ee963a1426d6094b40887.json\",\".tours/.memory/functions/find_memory_run_references.ts\",\".tours/.memory/functions/search_tours_memory_path.ts\",\"benchmarks/query-probe.mjs\",\"dist/citation-validator.js\",\"dist/cli.js\",\"dist/decomposition-prompt.js\",\"dist/exploration-evidence.js\",\"dist/exploration-helpers.js\",\"dist/explore.js\",\"dist/memory-output.js\",\"dist/memory.js\",\"dist/mistral.js\",\"dist/primitives.js\",\"dist/research-log.js\",\"dist/tool-contract.js\",\"dist/workspace.js\",\"package-lock.json\",\"package.json\",\"README.md\",\"skills/codetour-research/SKILL.md\",\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"src/cli.ts\",\"src/decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"src/exploration-evidence.ts\",\"src/exploration-helpers.ts\",\"src/explore.ts\",\"src/memory-output.ts\",\"src/memory.ts\",\"src/mistral.ts\",\"src/primitives.ts\",\"src/research-log.ts\",\"src/sandbox.d.ts\",\"src/tool-contract.ts\",\"src/workspace.ts\",\"test/citation-repair.test.ts\",\"test/citation-validator.test.ts\",\"test/cli.test.ts\",\"test/consolidation-d04.test.ts\",\"test/consolidation.test.ts\",\"test/empty-memory-list-note.test.ts\",\"test/explore.test.ts\",\"test/final-answer-fence-whitespace.test.ts\",\"test/final-answer-json-recovery.test.ts\",\"test/final-answer-recovery-visibility.test.ts\",\"test/finish-t02.test.ts\",\"test/fixture-explore.ts\",\"test/internal-instructions-english.test.ts\",\"test/memory.test.ts\"],\"returned\":50,\"observed\":61,\"truncated\":true,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":1388,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\",\"Output truncated to 50 items / 8000 bytes; it is NOT exhaustive. Re-run with narrower params to see the remainder.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"9lotBkQYg","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"readLines(\\\"src/citation-validator.ts\\\", 1, 120)\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"read_citation_validator\",\"question\":\"What does src/citation-validator.ts do regarding validation rules, refusal reasons, and interaction with tool history?\",\"description\":\"Reads the source of src/citation-validator.ts to extract exported functions, validation rules, refusal reasons, and how it interacts with tool history\",\"returns\":\"Lines of src/citation-validator.ts with file and line numbers\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"9lotBkQYg","content":"{\"error\":\"Script error: Invalid line range: use positive integer bounds and at most 100 lines\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"cqQEUqmHY","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"source\":\"readLines(\\\"src/citation-validator.ts\\\", 1, 100)\",\"params\":{},\"name\":\"read_citation_validator\",\"question\":\"What does src/citation-validator.ts do regarding validation rules, refusal reasons, and interaction with tool history?\",\"description\":\"Reads the source of src/citation-validator.ts to extract exported functions, validation rules, refusal reasons, and how it interacts with tool history\",\"returns\":\"Lines of src/citation-validator.ts with file and line numbers\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"cqQEUqmHY","content":"{\"result\":{\"file\":\"src/citation-validator.ts\",\"start\":1,\"lines\":[\"/**\",\" * Deterministic citation validation for function_try outputs\",\" * (issue #185, spec #183 — D02).\",\" *\",\" * Every mandatory reference a trial emits — any object carrying a `file`\",\" * field — is verified without any LLM: workspace confinement, file presence,\",\" * positive line bounds, startLine <= endLine, end within the real file, exact\",\" * excerpt equality when an excerpt is provided, and revision match when the\",\" * reference claims one. Partial validity is explicit: valid references stay\",\" * visible in the diagnostic and only the faulty ones are identified for\",\" * repair. The validator proves structural integrity only, never semantic\",\" * relevance — an existing citation is not proof of a business relation.\",\" */\",\"\",\"import { FileTooLargeError, PathOutsideWorkspaceError } from './primitives.ts';\",\"\",\"/** Confined read of the actual lines [startLine..endLine] plus the real total line count. */\",\"export interface CitationAccess {\",\"  readRange(file: string, startLine: number, endLine: number): Promise<{ lines: string[]; totalLines: number }>;\",\"}\",\"\",\"/** A single source reference: confined file path plus an exact line range. */\",\"export interface Reference {\",\"  file: string;\",\"  startLine: number;\",\"  endLine: number;\",\"}\",\"\",\"export interface InvalidCitation extends Partial<Reference> {\",\"  /** Short, structured, actionable error strings (type + path/line detail). */\",\"  errors: string[];\",\"}\",\"\",\"export interface CitationValidation {\",\"  /** 'valid' only when every emitted reference was verified; a failed trial is never treated as validated. */\",\"  status: 'valid' | 'validation_failed' | 'no_references';\",\"  /** Total mandatory references found in the output. */\",\"  references: number;\",\"  /** References actually verified (bounded by the safety ceiling). */\",\"  validated: number;\",\"  validCount: number;\",\"  /** Bounded list of the valid references (diagnostic visibility). */\",\"  validReferences: Reference[];\",\"  /** Bounded list of only the faulty references, for repair. */\",\"  invalidReferences: InvalidCitation[];\",\"  /** False when the ceiling stopped validation: the output is then NOT proven exhaustive. */\",\"  exhaustive: boolean;\",\"}\",\"\",\"/** Safety ceiling: at most this many references are verified per trial (configurable). */\",\"const MAX_REFERENCES = 300;\",\"/** Citation spans must fit a single confined read (workspace MAX_READ_LINES). */\",\"const MAX_SPAN_LINES = 100;\",\"/** Bounded diagnostic lists. */\",\"const MAX_LISTED = 10;\",\"/** Per-line excerpt truncation bounds of the permanent primitives (searchText/readLines: 2000, searchIdentifiers/findDefinitions: 500). */\",\"const EXCERPT_PREFIX_BOUNDS = [500, 2000];\",\"/** Fields that carry the reference's own excerpt — never recursed into as nested references. */\",\"const EXCERPT_KEYS = ['text', 'excerpt', 'lineText', 'lines'];\",\"\",\"/** Recursively collect every file-bearing object: those are the mandatory references. */\",\"function collectReferences(value: unknown, out: Record<string, unknown>[]): Record<string, unknown>[] {\",\"  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return out;\",\"  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\",\"    for (const child of value) collectReferences(child, out);\",\"    return out;\",\"  }\",\"  const record = value as Record<string, unknown>;\",\"  if (typeof record.file === 'string') out.push(record);\",\"  for (const [key, child] of Object.entries(record)) {\",\"    if (!EXCERPT_KEYS.includes(key)) collectReferences(child, out);\",\"  }\",\"  return out;\",\"}\",\"\",\"export async function validateCitations(value: unknown, options: { access: CitationAccess; revision?: string; maxReferences?: number }): Promise<CitationValidation> {\",\"  const references = collectReferences(value, []);\",\"  if (references.length === 0) {\",\"    return { status: 'no_references', references: 0, validated: 0, validCount: 0, validReferences: [], invalidReferences: [], exhaustive: true };\",\"  }\",\"  const ceiling = options.maxReferences ?? MAX_REFERENCES;\",\"  const invalid: InvalidCitation[] = [];\",\"  const valid: Reference[] = [];\",\"  let validated = 0;\",\"  for (const reference of references) {\",\"    if (validated >= ceiling) break;\",\"    validated++;\",\"    const check = await checkReference(reference, options);\",\"    if (check.invalid) invalid.push(check.invalid);\",\"    else valid.push(check.valid);\",\"  }\",\"  const exhaustive = validated === references.length;\",\"  if (!exhaustive) {\",\"    invalid.push({ errors: [`${references.length} references emitted; only ${validated} validated — the output is NOT proven exhaustive. Narrow the function output to at most ${ceiling} references and retry.`] });\",\"  }\",\"  return {\",\"    status: invalid.length > 0 ? 'validation_failed' : 'valid',\",\"    references: references.length,\",\"    validated,\",\"    validCount: valid.length,\"]},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":4856,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471