{"level":30,"time":1794911381620,"pid":12991,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"38a6cdfb-e199-4f4a-9dd6-a20b688b9b53","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"Structure and configuration of the logging system in src/research-log.ts, including pino logger setup, rotating-file-stream configuration, exact log file path (.tours/.log), and rotation policy\",\"Mechanism of runId generation and propagation across the codebase, including child logger creation and metadata attachment\",\"List of counters logged by the system (modelCalls, toolCalls, inputTokens, outputTokens, usageAvailable, memoryReuses) and their exact logging locations\",\"How memory persistence (.tours/.memory) interacts with logging and runIds, including consolidation gates and refusal signals\"],\"investigate\":[{\"action\":\"Read src/research-log.ts to extract logger configuration, file path, rotation settings, and child logger creation with runId metadata\",\"files\":[\"src/research-log.ts\"]},{\"action\":\"Search for runId generation in the codebase to identify where it is created and how it is structured\",\"files\":[\"src/*.ts\"]},{\"action\":\"Search for child logger usage with runId metadata to trace propagation\",\"files\":[\"src/*.ts\"]},{\"action\":\"Search for counter logging (modelCalls, toolCalls, inputTo