 primitive calls are impossible in this mode. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines}, and listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans ce workspace, comment le logging de recherche relie-t-il une exploration d'un run à ses traces persistées ? Détermine : (1) ce que fait src/research-log.ts (logger pino, rotating-file-stream, chemin exact .tours/.log, rotation), (2) comment le runId est généré et propagé (child logger, métadonnées), et (3) quels compteurs sont journalisés (modelCalls, toolCalls, inputTokens, outputTokens, usageAvailable, memoryReuses) et où la persistance de la mémoire entrelace logs et runIds. Produis